148
00:19:53,700 --> 00:20:06,750
In my opinion a period dependent intense metric for large portfolios it has its pros and cons.

149
00:20:06,750 --> 00:20:20,750
The disadvantage is that when you have a large portfolio you have different types of buildings under the influence of different earthquake response.

150
00:20:20,750 --> 00:20:31,750
So essentially to bring them all together under the same framework given a specific spectral acceleration value.

151
00:20:31,750 --> 00:20:41,750
It would be difficult that you have to do various spectral acceleration values like 0.3, 0.6, 1 second.

152
00:20:41,750 --> 00:20:47,750
So PGA or PGV which we use in that sense is robots.

153
00:20:47,750 --> 00:21:00,750
And I know from experience that PGV is sort of a better indicator for structural systems responding beyond the linear range.

154
00:21:00,750 --> 00:21:11,750
Which means if they start having more and more damage then PGV will show it better in a sense.

155
00:21:12,750 --> 00:21:21,750
So we also prefer using a non-period or period insensitive intense metric.

156
00:21:21,750 --> 00:21:29,750
